'''Breeding''' is a mechanic in {{PW}}. Through breeding you can get various [[Skills#Passive Skills|passive skills]] or [[Pal Subspecies]].

To breed Pals together you will need either a {{s|Breeding Farm}} or an {{s|Ancient Hatchery}}. Once you place the Breeding Farm of choice, you must assign a male and female [[Pals|Pal]]. The Breeding Farm also needs to be supplied with Cake. After some time they will produce a [[Pal Eggs|Pal Egg]] which can then be incubated.

== Cakes ==
* {{i|Cake}} - No additional effect.
* {{i|Mushroom Cake}} - Pals will have a slightly higher chance of having higher hidden stats.
* {{i|Vegetable Cake}} - Pals will produce two eggs instead of one.
* {{i|Extravagant Vegetable Cake}} - Mutations have a higher chance of occuring and higher chance of having better hidden stats.
* {{i|Special Cake}} - Higher chance of passing down the [[Passive Skills]] from their parents.

== How Breeding Works ==
The way breeding works is rather simple. Each Pal has a hidden breeding power number between 1 and 1500. The lower the number the more rare or powerful the Pal is. 

The game will then pick the Pal with the closest power to that average. As an example, if the baby Power ends up being 1015, and the closest values are 1010 ({{p|Felbat}}) and 1020 ({{p|Robinquill}}), the baby will be {{p|Robinquill}}. The 'tie breaker' (since 1015 is equal distance between 1010 and 1020) just comes down to the which Pal comes first in the game file's index. In this case {{p|Robinquill}} comes first in the game files so it gets picked over {{p|Felbat}}.

The way this works means you can never breed a Pal stronger/rarer than your strongest/rarest parent. For example, if your starting parents have a power of 570 ({{p|Anubis}}) and 1460 ({{p|Cattiva}}) the result will be the following: (570 + 1460) / 2 = 1015 ({{p|Robinquill}}).
If you then bred that baby at 1015 with your starting 570 {{p|Anubis}}: (570 + 1015) / 2 = 792.5 (which is closest to {{p|Croajiro}} at 795).

If you continue this multiple times:
*(570 + 795) / 2 = 682.5 ({{p|Univolt}} at 680)
*(570 + 680) / 2 = 625 ({{p|Omascul }} at 630)
*(570 + 625) / 2 = 597.5 ({{p|Incineram}} at 590)

As you can see you can get closer and closer to your 570 {{p|Anubis}} but you can never breed something stronger/rarer. But this also shows you can take one strong/rare Pal and breed it with its offspring and quickly start making Pals near that strength.

== Mutation ==
Mutation is a random occurance which can happen to eggs being bred. The chance of it happening seems to be around 1%. This can be boosted with an {{i|Extravagant Vegetable Cake}}.

A mutated Egg will always be a different outcome to what the parents normally would produce and will always have a mutation-exclusive [[Passive Skills|Passive Skill]].

